    "note": "supply = xi f_esc N_gamma_eff per ISM baryon per Gyr; demand = alpha_B n_e. The balance point n_e,crit is the depth to which the diffuse column stays ionized. The VMO branch sustains ionization to ~5e2-2e7 x n_b0 across the scanned plane, straddling the ~500x rise required at the opacity-boundary depth; the standard branch saturates ~25x shallower, failing the deepest requirement at the conservative corner. Ionization is a maintained equilibrium, not an epoch: the ionized column the opacity theorem requires is supplied by the same stellar budget, with the VMO-enhanced yield the factor that reaches the required depth under pessimistic escape/cycling."
