    "note": "f_VMO_min solves xi f_esc [f N_VMO + (1-f) N_std] = alpha_B n_e. Over most of the plane the standard yield already suffices at this depth (f_VMO_min = 0): the ionization sector adds no countervailing bound on the helium requirement. Toward the conservative corner (xi <= 1e-2/Gyr and f_esc <= 0.1) f_VMO_min rises to ~0.07-1.0, and at the extreme corner (xi = 1e-3/Gyr, f_esc = 0.01) the 500x depth is marginal even at f_VMO = 1 (97% of the requirement). The constraint therefore directionally favours the high-VMO branch the helium fixed point requires \u2014 supportive, not exclusionary."
