    "note": "Under the p = 0.5 horizon law at constant n_e = n_b0 the Thomson tau = 1 surface sits at z ~ 20 (the Step-11 sigma_T row), and the partial column accumulated in the optically thin approach is ~0.053 by z ~ 4 \u2014 the Planck tau_reion = 0.054 magnitude. A mild density rise (m = 0.5) reaches the same wing amplitude by z ~ 3 with the tau = 1 surface at z ~ 11.6; the observed wing therefore selects a near-flat to mildly-rising approach profile. The low-EE wing is the approach column of the single opacity boundary, not evidence of a discrete reionization epoch; its precise amplitude is a datum on the n_e(ell) approach profile, owned by the absorber-statistics inversion of the opacity programme (three-point requirement)."
