  "F_qualitative_closures": {
    "star_formation_history": "None to contradict: the VMO branch is a metallicity-selected channel (Z < Z_crit ~ 1e-4) that is local and asynchronous across patches; in the eternal steady state there is no global Pop III chronology.",
    "background_light": "All processed starlight \u2014 including the hard VMO spectrum \u2014 enters the Step-11 thermalization bath; the divergent column reprocesses any input spectrum into the blackbody (achromatic shear invariance), so no separate EBL budget arises.",
    "photon_escape": "VMO ionizing radiation is emitted over the ~2-3 Myr main sequence before core collapse forms the temporal horizon; the horizon sequesters the metal-bearing remnant, not the emitted radiation field.",
    "depth_correlation": "Where the demand is highest (deep, dense sightlines), patches are youngest and most metal-poor, so the local f_VMO(Z) transition concentrates the enhanced VMO yield exactly where the 500x recombination demand applies."
  },
  "verdict": "Steady-state ionization balance closes: the f_VMO = 0.994 branch sustains the ionized diffuse column to n_e ~ 5e2-2e7 x n_b0 across the scanned (xi, f_esc) plane \u2014 bracketing the ~500x rise the opacity boundary requires \u2014 so the reionization/optical-depth sector adds no countervailing bound on the helium-driven VMO fraction and mildly favours it at the conservative corner. The tau_reion = 0.054 datum is the approach wing of the single opacity boundary (constant-density baseline: tau ~ 0.05 accumulated by z ~ 4), with its profile-shape content assigned to the absorber inversion, not an epoch budget the VMO population must meet."
}